          "path": "_m/9/y/z/s/st-charles-missouri-wp/st-charles-missouri-bp.jpg",
          "filename": "St Charles MO BPOE.JPG",
          "caption": "St. Charles, Missouri BPOE (Elks Club) at 122 S. Main.  This is part of the  St. Charles Historic District, on the NRHP since September 22, 1970.  The boundaries are as messy as any HD on the NRHP, but it basically goes from Adams Street in the north to Chauncey - Boone's Lick Rd in the south, along the Missouri River for about 1.5 miles, and inland to 2nd Street, including Main Street.\n\nOfficial boundaries are roughly bounded by the Missouri River and Madison, Chauncey, and 2nd Sts.; also 1000 S. Main St.; also bounded by Madison, 2nd, Jefferson, and the alley behind the 100 block of S. Main St.; also the 100, 200, and 300 blocks of N. Main St., in St. Charles\tSecond, third, and fourth sets of boundaries represent boundary increases of June 4, 1987, May 1, 1991, and October 10, 1996 respectively",
          "alt": "St. Charles, Missouri BPOE (Elks Club) at 122 S. Main.  This is part of the  St. Charles Historic District, on the NRHP since September 22, 1970.  The boundaries are as messy as any HD on the NRHP, but it basically goes from Adams Street in the north to Chauncey - Boone's Lick Rd in the south, along the Missouri River for about 1.5 miles, and inland to 2nd Street, including Main Street.\n\nOfficial boundaries are roughly bounded by the Missouri River and Madison, Chauncey, and 2nd Sts.; also 1000 S. Main St.; also bounded by Madison, 2nd, Jefferson, and the alley behind the 100 block of S. Main St.; also the 100, 200, and 300 blocks of N. Main St., in St. Charles\tSecond, third, and fourth sets of boundaries represent boundary increases of June 4, 1987, May 1, 1991, and October 10, 1996 respectively",
          "width": 2767,
